{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":372676,"duration_api_ms":113303,"ttft_ms":2726,"ttft_stream_ms":1643,"time_to_request_ms":18,"num_turns":14,"result":"This confirms it: the actual minutes-remaining/cost estimate (`emit(\"LALAL preflight: ... minutes remaining; estimated ... minutes ...\")`) is only produced inside `separate()` at `src/vgt/separation.py:718-724`, which executes *after* the CLI has already collected consent (`cli.py:94-99`). At consent time the user only sees an operation count (\"N operations will be submitted\"), not an actual cost/minutes figure — despite the message even saying \"LALAL will report the authoritative minute estimate ... before any submission,\" implying the number arrives later, after the user already said yes.\n\nThis directly violates the issue's explicit acceptance requirement: *\"Before spending: print remaining minutes, estimated operation cost, and cached vs outstanding operations\"* and *\"`--force-stems` cannot spend without cost disclosure + explicit consent.\"* Consent here is not actually informed by cost — it's a blind \"yes\" to an unknown number of minutes.\n\nNote the local audio file's duration is available on disk before any network call (`status.py` already reads WAV duration locally via the `wave` module), so an estimated-minutes figure could be computed and shown pre-consent without needing a network round-trip — this is a fixable gap, not an inherent limitation of the API.\n\nREJECT\n\n### VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n- `git diff main...HEAD` — reviewed full implementation of CLI wiring, `separation_preview`, `separate`, and `status.py` changes.\n- `uv run pytest -q` — 101 passed, 3 warnings, no failures.\n- `src/vgt/cli.py:81-99` — consent prompt (`--force-stems` interactive `yes`/`--accept-stem-cost`) fires with only an operation *count* displayed (`preview[\"outstanding_operations\"]`), no minutes-remaining or cost figure.\n- `src/vgt/separation.py:713-724` — the actual `remaining_minutes`/`estimated_minutes` preflight message is emitted only inside `separate()`, which the CLI calls *after* consent has already been obtained (`cli.py:100-107`).\n- Issue body / `docs/stem-separation-plan.md` §3-C — explicitly requires: *\"Before spending, print remaining minutes, estimated operation cost, and cached/outstanding operations\"* and *\"an exact operation/cost preview + interactive confirmation.\"*\n\n### VERDICT REASON\nThe paid-work confirmation flow does not meet the issue's cost-disclosure requirement. `--force-stems` (interactively or via `--accept-stem-cost`) lets the user consent to spending before any minutes-remaining or estimated-cost number has been shown — only a count of outstanding operations is displayed pre-consent. The actual \"LALAL preflight: X minutes remaining; estimated Y minutes\" message is emitted later, inside `separate()`, i.e. after consent has already been given. This is a blind consent, not the \"exact operation/cost preview\" the issue and plan explicitly call for.\n\nFix: compute and display an estimated cost before the confirmation prompt — e.g. read the local reference source's duration (already done elsewhere via the `wave` module in `status.py`) to estimate minutes needed for the outstanding operations, and/or call `LalalSeparator.remaining_minutes()` (already exposed) before prompting, so the user sees both the account's remaining minutes and an estimated operation cost prior to typing \"yes\" or passing `--accept-stem-cost`.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f20fb3bf-c7a7-4967-846e-0474e11daa06","total_cost_usd":0.6868155999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":14699,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51866,"cache_read_input_tokens":739012,"output_tokens":7226,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens"